  "notes": "Pinckneyville pressing with gold \"MCA RECORDS\" below the Backstreet logo on labels. \nAnother Pinckneyville pressing exists with \"MCA RECORDS\" in black lettering below the Backstreet logo here: [r4385615]\n\nRecorded at Sound City, Van Nuys, Ca. and Cherokee Studios, Hollywood, Ca.\nMixed at Cherokee and Record Plant, N.Y.C.\nMastered at Sterling Sound, NYC\n\nIncludes custom printed sturdy inner picture sleeve with album credits on back.\n\n\"◈-P-◈\" stamp in runouts denotes an MCA-Pinckneyville pressing.\n\"STERLING\" stamp in runouts denotes Sterling Sound cutting.\n\n© 1979 Backstreet Records, A Division of MCA Records, Inc.\n℗ 1979 Backstreet Records, A Division of MCA Records, Inc.\nPrinted in U.S.A.\n\nOn label rim:\nMFD & DISTRIB. BY MCA DISTRIB. CORP., 100 UNIVERSAL CITY PLAZA, UNIVERSAL CITY, CA 91608\n\nAll songs published by Skyhill Publishing Co., Inc. BMI",
